<title>USA: Standard Products sets plant-closing charge.</title>
<headline>Standard Products sets plant-closing charge.</headline>
<dateline>DEARBORN 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Standard Products Co on Thursday said it would record a charge of $17.7 million, or $0.63 a share, against earnings for the third quarter of fiscal 1997 for the closings of two automotive parts plants.</p>
<p>Late last month, Standard Products said it would close a 224,000-square-foot plastics products plant in Schenectady, N.Y., by the end of the year, and a 115,000-square-foot sealing systems plant in Lexington, Ky., by the end of August.</p>
